.TH LT-QWWAD_SPIN_FLIP_RAMAN "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_spin_flip_raman (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_spin_flip_raman \- find the spin-flip Raman spectrum.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_spin_flip_raman
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the spin\-flip Raman spectrum.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-l\fR [ \fB\-\-linewidth\fR ] arg (=1)
Linewidth of all transitions [cm^{\-1}].
.TP
\fB\-s\fR [ \fB\-\-wavenumbermin\fR ] arg (=0)
Minimum wavenumber for spectrum [cm^{\-1}].
.HP
\fB\-u\fR [ \fB\-\-wavenumbermax\fR ] arg (=100) Maximum wavenumber for spectrum [cm^{\-1}].
.TP
\fB\-t\fR [ \fB\-\-wavenumberstep\fR ] arg (=1)
Step in wavenumber for spectrum [cm^{\-1}].
.TP
\fB\-\-spinflipfile\fR arg (=e_sf.r)
Table of spin\-flip energies vs donor
position.
.TP
\fB\-\-spectrumfile\fR arg (=I.r)
Filename for output spectrum.
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'e_sf.r'   Spin-flip energy table:
              Column 1: donor location [Angstrom]
              Column 2: Spin-flip energy [meV]

.SS Output files:
   'I.r'      Spin-flip Raman spectrum:
              Column 1: Energy [1/cm]
              Column 2: Intensity [arb. units]
.SH EXAMPLES

Find the spin-flip Raman spectrum in the energy range 10-30/cm using 1/cm step and 3/cm linewidth:
    qwwad_spin_flip_raman --wavenumbermin 10 --wavenumbermax 30 --wavenumberstep 1 --linewidth 3
.SH "SPECTRAL MODEL"
This program calculates a hypothetical spin-flip Raman
spectrum assuming a uniform distribution of dopants at the
positions given in the input file, and assigning a Gaussian intensity curve to each one.
The total signal is therefore a simple sum of Gaussians.
